{
"from": 229,
"to": 232,
"text": "The gates are the standing lint and unit entries; one unit filter and one integration filter that select what this chunk adds; a preservation guard; the harness smoke with G2 and G4 over its home; the native `pre-push`; and the operator's hygiene, push and CI read (`leg = 'operator'`, the `ci.py conclusion` call, `inputs#I1` note 6)."
},
{
"from": 234,
"to": 236,
"text": "No mutation entry, no witness run and no workflow dispatch is listed (`inputs#I1` note 1). No entry is a live leg: nothing starts the real `claude`. Step 14's readings are implement's, in `evidence/red-green.md`, and are never an entry. The operator entries are held by step 15."
},
{
"from": 238,
"to": 243,
"text": "The smoke boots an ordinary `viola run` session, so the start goes through the gate's first evaluation and the harness's own readiness check reads `budget-gate` as record two. The preservation guard names the base commit, because the operator pass's pre-CI commit moves HEAD onto the chunk. It is what shows that no ledger row, no Claude shape, no schema value, no fixture, no fake-agent option and no harness file moved; it lists no file a step edits. If the review card keeps the harness flag in this chunk, the guard loses `crates/viola-e2e` in the same revision."
}
],
